>Anyone else of the opinion that wraith corpses are WAY too powerful?
>They're easy kills, and once you have the cursed Bell you're
>guaranteed level 30 in no time.
>
>It would make the game a lot more challenging if this
>'free level' were taken out, or at least make the chance
>to be drained a lot higher.
>
>Comments?

Here are some ideas on ways this might be changed in future releases:
 1. Correlate the probabliltiy of a wraith leaving a corpse to the
    player's level.  Wraith corpses should be rare and hard to find
    by the time the player's level gets into the mid 20s.
 2. Have wraith corpses spoil rapidly.
 3. Make wraith corpses very filling - once you've eaten one, you'll
    have a hard time getting another one down anytime soon and will run
    the risk of choking to death if you try.
 4. Use an algorithm for experience gained such that starting at about
    level 20, more than one wraith corpse is required to gain a level.
    The number required increases with each successive level.  This might
    also apply to potions of gain level, though perhaps the latter would
    work better, especially if blessed.
As it is now, once you get to the upper teens and beyond, the number of
experience points needed to advance to the next level gets way too big,
to the point where it is not feasable to gain levels by killing monsters
anymore (only by eating wraith corpses and drinking potions of gain
level).  Having an exponential relationship between level and experience
works okay up to about level 10, but after that I think it should taper
off to a polynomial relationship.

